  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ITL-Gender Transformative Climate Resilient Microfinance Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is focused on integrating climate change adaptation and strengthening gender transformative approaches in the existing microfinance members of the partner &#x2013; Ganna Unnayan Kendra. The project is designed based on the experience and data that beneficiary selection, disbursement and activity implemented don&#x2019;t take climate risk into their process. At the same time, women, the majority of borrowers, don&#x2019;t have a say in deciding on the choice of activities and how the loan amount will be utilised. The project focuses on the following approaches: a. Integrating climate change and gender transformative approach to microfinance. b. Protecting assets of most vulnerable families (around 25% borrowers) from extreme climate risk by strengthening/ mitigating risk activities and linking with social protection schemes of the Govt. c. documentation of guidelines/ tools developed and sharing them with other stakeholders and GUK staff. d. Developing key learning questions, identifying lessons learnt, and sharing with the stakeholders who will take forward the initiative.
The project has innovation in refining existing processes and integrating climate change risk &amp; adaptation during the entire cycle of microfinance. The project has built-in research and learning events (such as review meetings, analysis of the microfinance data, etc.) The experiences from the project can be scaled up across the country since microfinance operations cover around 50% of the population.</narrative>
  </description>
